          "content": "You are playing a grid rearrangement puzzle.\n\nTHE GRID:\n- The board is an 8×8 grid. Rows are labelled R1–R8 (top to bottom), columns C1–C8 (left to right).\n- The board is given to you as compact listings, refreshed every turn:\n  - CURRENT BOARD has an `Objects:` line listing each object as `Label@RrowCcol` (e.g. `Objects: A@R1C1 B@R2C3`), and, when there are walls, a `Walls:` line (e.g. `Walls: R4C4 R5C6`).\n  - GOAL BOARD is a `Targets:` line listing your objects' target cells as `Label->RrowCcol` (e.g. `Targets: A->R3C5`).\n- Any cell not listed as an object or a wall is empty. Objects cannot enter wall cells or leave the grid.\n\nYOUR TASK:\nMove all objects to their target positions. The GOAL BOARD shows where each object must end up.\nYou control ALL objects on the board: A, B, C, D, E, F. You may move any of them on any turn.\n\nRULES:\n- On each turn, move exactly ONE object exactly ONE cell: up, down, left, or right.\n- Objects CANNOT move into wall cells or outside the grid boundaries.\n- Two objects CANNOT occupy the same cell.\n\nRESPONSE FORMAT:\nYou must respond using exactly this format, no other text:\nBegin your response directly with `move:` on the very first line. Do not output any preamble, thinking, or scratchpad text before it.\nmove: <OBJECT> <DIRECTION>\n\nExample:\nmove: A right\n\nThe game ends automatically as soon as every object is on its target cell.\n\n\nCURRENT BOARD:\nObjects: A@R4C1 B@R5C3 C@R6C5 D@R8C4 E@R7C2 F@R6C7\n\nGOAL BOARD (where each object must end up):\nTargets: A->R1C8 B->R2C8 C->R4C8 D->R6C1 E->R2C4 F->R3C8",
